# Anti-Patterns

Canonical source for Claude/Codex parity: `.claude/rules/anti-patterns.md`.

## Core

1. switch/case - use match() or Record<Key, Value> lookup
2. try/catch for flow control - use attempt() with [data, err] tuple
3. `as` type assertions - use type narrowing, guards, or discriminated unions
4. `?.` / `??` on non-optional types - trust types, use ensurePresent()
5. Hardcoded magic values - use named constants or convertDuration()
6. useMemo/useCallback - React Compiler handles memoization

## quantum-vault-Specific

7. Hardcoded hex colors - use theme tokens
8. if (isLoading) manual checks - use MatchQuery
9. Generic components/ folder - use feature-based organization
10. Altering provider order without explicit architecture scope
11. Silent early returns in user-action handlers
12. Bypassing ScreenProvider hydration flow
